{
  "raw": {
    "https://cuny.jobs/0FC1D23010F146F28EA332DAB61D321325": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor /Associate Professor - Clinical Practices and Special Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor /Associate Professor - Clinical Practices and Special Education. Assistant Professor /Associate Professor - Clinical Practices and Special Education **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Middle and High School Education (MHSE) invites applications for a tenure track Assistant Professor /Associate ProfessorClinical Practices and Special Education-grades 7-12. The Department of Middle and High School Education (MHSE) in the School of Education at Lehman College, City University of New York (Bronx, New York City) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor of clinical practices in secondary teacher education and adolescent special education (and/or a related field). The successful candidate must demonstrate excellence in teaching, service, advocacy, leadership, and research in special education and teacher candidate practices leading to the implementation of evidence-based strategies that effectively support diverse learners with disabilities in real classroom settings across all subject areas at the secondary school level. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate knowledge and skills for teaching undergraduate and graduate-level courses (on campus and online) in multiple modalities. The successful candidate will also be expected to advise students, engage in and maintain an active program of research, scholarly work (including professional publications, presentations, grantsmanship), and service. The successful candidate also shares responsibility for committee and department assignments, performing administrative, supervisory, and other functions as assigned. This position reports directly to the chairperson of Middle and High School Education (MHSE). This is not a remote position. While some online teaching or remote administrative work may be allowed, the role requires consistent on-campus engagement. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular on-campus presence for teaching, office hours, departmental and other activities. About Lehman College School of Education (SOE) Lehman College of The City University of New York is CUNYs only senior college in the borough of the Bronx. A federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution, Lehman serves a diverse population of more than 14,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The School of Education (SOE) is one of the six schools within Lehman College. The SOE reflects the mission of the college in serving the Bronx, New York City, and surrounding region as an intellectual, economic, and cultural center. As the only public higher education school of education in the Bronx, SOE embraces a vision of preparing future educators to meet the needs of an increasingly diverse student population who themselves represent a racial, ethnic, cultural, and linguistic spectrum that remains one of the strengths of our state and community. SOE is organized in three departments: Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE); Counseling, Leadership, Literacy, and Special Education (CLLSE); and Middle and High School Education (MHSE). SOE offers initial preparation advanced preparation programs in Literacy Studies, Mental Health and Educational Leadership, including a doctorate in Organizational Leadership. SOE houses several institutes and centers to advance educator preparation, professional development, and schoolcommunity engagement. MHSE has nationally recognized and accredited undergraduate and graduate programs that prepare candidates to earn New York State teacher certifications in secondary content areas (English, Foreign Languages, Mathematics, Science, and Social Studies) as well as Dance P-12, ESOL P-12, Visual Arts P-12, Music P-12, and the Bilingual Extension 5-12. Faculty in the department are committed to the Lehman Urban Transformative Education framework adopted by Lehman's School of Education. Our goal is to prepare innovative and creative educators who inspire, influence and value others. We believe in the rich contribution of each of our educational partners in shaping our transformative practice. Position Responsibilities In a spirit of collegiality and professionalism, faculty are expected to foster a respectful, collaborative, and inclusive environment, upholding high ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. They are expected to work cooperatively toward the growth and development of their department and support student success. Opportunities are available for faculty development and travel awards. Lehman College and CUNY internal funding is available through competitive grants for scholarship and professional development support. Responsibilities include: Maintaining a teaching load of 18 credits per 9-month academic year. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular on-campus presence for teaching, office hours, departmental, and other activities. This includes collaborating with the SOE Cinical Practice and Partnership Office and other units to participate in and to facilitate off-campus site visits to partner schools to monitor and support the successful implementation of clinically rich, school-based placements and to strengthen collaborative relationships with school partners. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda that includes professional scholarship, presentations and grantsmanship. Other responsibilities include: Engage in student recruitment, application review, and admissions processes. Support department and program operations and coordination to ensure effective student advisement, placement, and supervision. Collaborate with faculty and staff across departments, schools, and the university to advance interdisciplinary and sponsored program initiatives Engage in program-level and SOE accreditation Pursue external funding opportunities to support research, program innovation, and continuous improvement efforts for themselves as researchers, the Department, the SOE, Lehman College, and the field. Develop and maintain articulation agreements and educational partnerships with community colleges. Engage in service to the university, college, school, and department through committee membership and related professional contributions Assist with program hiring, staffing, mentoring, and supervision of part-time and adjunct faculty Perform other related duties as assigned in support of program and institutional goals **QUALIFICATIONS** Required Qualifications Ph.D. or Ed.D. degree in Special Education or a closely related field from an accredited university Demonstrated expertise in mentoring pre- and in-service teacher development in clinical settings, educational assessment, experiential learning, and project-based learning Demonstracted knowledge of best-pratices in urban secondary teacher education pre-service and in-service clinical and teacher induction practices A minimum of five years of teaching experience teaching in public, secondary schools with diverse populations, including multilingual students. Ongoing record of scholarship Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member Preferred Requirements: Demonstrated commitment to social justice, multi-modal learning, anti-racist pedagogies, multilingualism, and culturally and linguistically responsive and sustaining pedagogy Demonstrated knowledge of Students With Disabilites 7-12 learning standards and curricula Demonstrated ability to effectively teach adults in college level education programs in various modalities including in person, hybrid, hyflex, synchronous and asynchronous modalities. Lehman College will not be accepting/interviewing individuals who are presently outside of the United States who require an H1B visa. Applicants currently residing in the United States who require H-1B visa sponsorship are eligible to be interviewed. **COMPENSATION** Assistant $86,741 -$102,017 Associate $ $105,816 - $121,194 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach a resume, cover letter, and three professional references (name, title, organization, and contact information). **CLOSING DATE** OPEN UNTIL FILLED: The review of applications will begin immediately and continue until a candidate has been identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32296 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/4C9780C9508B4E919132280714D8951725": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor /Associate Professor -  Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor /Associate Professor - Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE). Assistant Professor /Associate Professor - Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE) in the School of Education at Lehman College, City University of New York (Bronx, New York City) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in literacies with a focus on how technology and digital literacies play a role in childrens development, and/or a related field. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellence in teaching, service, advocacy, and leadership in childhood education, as well as digital literacies development, to engage and inspire our economically, culturally, and linguistically diverse candidates, colleagues, and kindergarten6th grade partnership schools. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate knowledge and skills for teaching undergraduate and graduate-level courses (on campus and online) in multiple modalities within the child development age range, literacies development and/or the humanities. The successful candidate will also be expected to advise students, engage in and maintain an active program of research, scholarly work (including professional publications, presentations, grantsmanship), and service. This position reports directly to the chairperson of Early Childhood and Childhood Education (ECCE). This is not a remote position. While some online teaching or remote administrative might be allowed, the role requires consistent on-campus engagement. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular presence for teaching, office hours, departmental and other activities About Lehman College School of Education (SOE) Lehman College of The City University of New York is CUNYs only senior college in the borough of the Bronx. A federally designated Hispanic Serving Institution, Lehman serves a diverse population of more than 14,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The School of Education (SOE) is one of the six schools within Lehman College. The SOE reflects the mission of the college in serving the Bronx, New York City, and surrounding region as an intellectual, economic, and cultural center. As the only public higher education school of education in the Bronx, SOE embraces a vision of preparing future educators to meet the needs of an increasingly diverse student population who themselves represent a racial, ethnic, cultural, and linguistic spectrum that remains one of the strengths of our state and community. SOE is organized in three departments: Early Childhood and Childhood Education; Counseling, Leadership, Literacy, and Special Education (CLLSE); and Middle and High School Education. SOE offers initial preparation advanced preparation programs in Literacy Studies, Mental Health and Educational Leadership, including a doctorate in Organizational Leadership. SOE houses several institutes and centers to advance educator preparation, professional development, and schoolcommunity engagement. ECCE houses outstanding and nationally accredited graduate degree programs, with each culminating in a masters degree, or an advanced certificate, and most leading to New York State Certification. It also offers an Infant/Toddler certificate and the Advanced Bilingual Extension. Our faculty are committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching and are recognized for their work with Bronx and urban schools, districts, nonprofits, and other community organizations, and strive to provide transformational learning experiences for our graduate students. They are experienced in meeting the needs of adult learners and are dedicated to mentoring, motivating, and supporting our graduate students through consistent advisement, engaging instruction, continuous program improvement, and career placement. Position Responsibilities In a spirit of collegiality and professionalism, faculty are expected to foster a respectful, collaborative, and inclusive environment, upholding high ethical standards in teaching, research, and service. They are expected to work cooperatively toward the growth and development of their department and support student success. Responsibilities include: Maintaining a teaching load of 18 credits per 9-month academic year. Teaching assignments include undergraduate and graduate-level courses in child development, pedagogical foundations, as well as teaching methods across the humanities delivered on campus and online across multiple instructional modalities within the Childhood Education curriculum. The successful candidate will maintain an active research agenda that includes professional scholarship, presentations and grantsmanship The successful candidate will share responsibility for continuous program improvement and program accreditation (including AAQEP compliance), academic advisement, and department assignments, including administrative duties, program and course development. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular on-campus presence for teaching, office hours, departmental, and other activities. Other responsibilities include: -Program coordination - Engage in student recruitment, application review, and admissions processes. -Support department and program operations and coordination to ensure effective student advisement, placement, and supervision. -Collaborate with faculty and staff across departments and schools to advance interdisciplinary and sponsored program initiatives. -Pursue external funding opportunities to support research, program innovation, and continuous improvement efforts for themselves as researchers, the Department, the School of Education, Lehman College, and the field. -Develop and maintain articulation agreements and educational partnerships with community colleges. -Engage in service to the university, college, school, and department through committee membership and related professional contributions. -Assist with program hiring, staffing, mentoring, and supervision of part-time and adjunct faculty. -Perform other related duties as assigned in support of program and institutional goals. **QUALIFICATIONS** Required Qualifications -Ph.D. or Ed.D. degree in Education or a closely related field from an accredited university. -Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and/or graduate-level teaching foundation courses in education, as well as teaching methods courses through in-person and online modalities. -Experience in teaching in educational settings that serve teachers and children. -A minimum of five years of teaching experience teaching in elementary schools with diverse populations, including multilingual students. Strong commitment to social justice, anti-racism, and anti-oppression, diversity, equity, and inclusion -Ongoing record of scholarship. -Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member. Preferred Requirements: -Experience teaching courses in childhood development, pedagogical/curriculum development, methods of literacies, including digital literacies and/or social studies. -Experience in program development, curriculum and assessment design, infusing digital literacies and technologies across the curriculum, mentoring teacher development. -Experience in assessment, recruitment, and/or advisement. Lehman College will not be accepting/interviewing individuals who are presently outside of the United States who require an H1B visa. Applicants currently residing in the United States who require H-1B visa sponsorship are eligible to be interviewed. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor: $ 86,741 - $102,017 (PSC 9/1/2025) Associate Professor: $105,816 - $121,194 (PSC 9/1/2025) CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach a resume, cover letter, and three professional references (name, title, organization, and contact information). **CLOSING DATE** The review of applicants will begin immediately. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32295 Location: Lehman College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/7CA71701A90D4FDA8369EDA1FF4F393A25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics. Assistant Professor of Political Science - Specialization in American Politics **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelors, masters, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The Colleges community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The Department of Political Science at Lehman College, The City University of New York, invites applications for an Assistant Professor in American politics, beginning Fall 2027. We welcome applications from scholars across the field, and are especially interested in candidates whose research and teaching engage one or more of the following areas: public law, including constitutional law, law and courts, law and society, and American constitutional development; immigration law, policy, and politics, including citizenship; criminal justice and civil rights; American political behavior and institutions, including elections, public opinion, parties, and political participation; American political development; and the intersection of technology and politics, including artificial intelligence. A central service responsibility for the position will be pre-law advising. The appointee will serve as the departments pre-law advisor and will lead the pre-law program, departmental internships, and the minor in Law and Government. Candidates must be able to teach the departments introductory course on American government and politics. Responsibilities of the academic appointment include maintaining an active program of scholarship and a robust publication record; developing courses and curriculum and teaching introductory and advanced undergraduate courses; and service to the department and full participation in the life of the College and the University. Obtaining grant funding to support research and institutional initiatives is encouraged. Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member are also important. The faculty member may have the opportunity to become involved in graduate programs (masters and PhD level) at the CUNY Graduate Center. The appointment requires regular on-campus presence for teaching, advising, office hours, and departmental and College activities, although some online teaching or remote administrative work may be involved. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D. in Political Science or related field or J.S.D./S.J.D., in hand by start date. Preferred: J.D./Ph.D.; experience with or commitment to pre-law advising and mentoring students toward legal and public careers; a robust record of teaching and research. Also required are the ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. **COMPENSATION** $98,231 - $112,841 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Applicants should be prepared to submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, writing samples, and evidence of teaching effectiveness (e.g. sample syllabi, summary of teaching evaluations, teaching statement). Letters of recommendation will be requested for candidates advanced to the semi-finalist round. Review of applications will begin in early October 2026 and continue until the position is filled. Please direct questions to joseph.mohorcich@lehman.cuny.edu and elhum.haghighat@lehman.cuny.edu. **CLOSING DATE** Applications to be received until November 2nd, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32747 Location: Lehman College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/EA4B0720084E4327B41A530BC02E9D9625": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Special Education",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Special Education. Assistant Professor - Special Education **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic-Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelors, masters, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The Colleges community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The School of Education (SOE) is one of the six schools within Lehman College. SOE reflects the mission of the college in serving the Bronx, New York City, and surrounding region as an intellectual, economic, and cultural center. As the only public higher education school of education in the Bronx, SOE embraces a vision of preparing future educators to meet the needs of increasingly diverse student population who themselves represent a racial, ethnic, cultural, and linguistic spectrum that remains one of the strengths of our state and community. SOE is organized in three departments: Early Childhood and Childhood Education; Counseling, Leadership, Literacy, and Special Education (CLLSE); and Middle and High School Education. SOE offers initial preparation programs that include Early Childhood Education, Childhood Education, English Education, Foreign Language, Science Education, Mathematics Education, Social Studies Education, TESOL, Literacy, and Special Education across grades. Bilingual Extensions in most certification areas is also offered. SOE also collaborates with the schools of Arts and Humanities and Health Sciences, Human Services, and Nursing in offering initial preparation programs in Music Education, Art Education, and Health Education. SOE offers two advanced preparation programs in Literacy Studies, Mental Health and Educational Leadership, including a doctorate in Organizational Leadership. SOE houses several institutes and centers to advance educator preparation, professional development, and schoolcommunity engagement. CLLSE houses a variety of outstanding and nationally accredited graduate degree programs, with each culminating in a doctoral degree, or masters degree, or an advanced certificate, and most leading to New York State Certification. Our faculty are committed to excellence in scholarship and teaching and are recognized for their work with Bronx and urban schools, districts, nonprofits, and other community organizations, and strive to provide transformational learning experiences for our graduate students. They are experienced in meeting the needs of adult learners and are dedicated to mentoring, motivating, and supporting our graduate students through consistent advisement, engaging instruction, continuous program improvement, and career placement. The Department of Counseling, Leadership, Literacy, and Special Education (CLLSE) in the School of Education at Lehman College, City University of New York (Bronx, New York City) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor in Special Education. The successful candidate must demonstrate excellence in teaching, service, advocacy, and research in the field of Special Education to engage and inspire our economically, culturally, and linguistically diverse candidates, colleagues, and P20 schools. The successful candidate will be expected to demonstrate knowledge and skills for teaching graduate-level courses (on campus and online) in multiple modalities within the Special Education curriculum. Candidate may also be assigned to teach undergraduate courses and advise undergraduate students. The successful candidate will be expected to advise students, engage in and maintain an active program of research, scholarly work (including professional publications and presentations), service, and overall, maintain professional identity as a Special Educator. Excellent administrative and interpersonal skills are required. Familiarity with accreditation at the higher education level is helpful. This position reports directly to the chairperson of CLLSE. **Position Responsibilities:** Responsibilities include maintaining a teaching load of 18 credits per 9-month academic year. Teaching assignments include graduate-level and undergraduate courses delivered on campus and online across multiple instructional modalities within the Special Education curriculum. The successful candidate will share responsibility for continuous program improvement and program accreditation, academic advisement, and department assignments, including administrative duties, program and course development. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular on campus presence for teaching, office hours, departmental and other activities. In addition to eighteen (18) teaching hours per year, you are required to engage in research, scholarship, and service. You may be assigned to teach evenings and/or weekends, and/or online, either synchronously or asynchronously. This is not a remote position. Other responsibilities include: + Engage in student recruitment, application review, and admissions processes + Engage in program assessment, accreditation activities, and ongoing program development and improvement initiatives + Support department and program operations and clinical coordination to ensure effective student placement and supervision + Collaborate with faculty and staff across departments and schools to advance interdisciplinary and sponsored program initiatives + Pursue external funding opportunities to support research, program innovation, and continuous improvement efforts + Develop and maintain articulation agreements and educational partnerships with schools and other external organizations and institutions. + Engage in service to the university, college, school, and department through committee membership and related professional contributions + Assist with program hiring, staffing, mentoring, and supervision of part-time and adjunct faculty. + Perform other related duties as assigned in support of program and institutional goals **QUALIFICATIONS** Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Special Education or related degree + Demonstrated excellence in graduate-level teaching through in-person and online modalities. + Experience working with diverse student populations. Strong commitment to social justice, anti-racism, and anti-oppression, diversity, equity, and inclusion + Ongoing record of scholarship. + Strong organizational and interpersonal skills and the ability to work collegially as a team member. **COMPENSATION** $89,777 - $105,588. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach a resume, cover letter, and three professional references (name, title, organization, and contact information). **CLOSING DATE** The review of applications will begin on October 20th, 2026 until a candidate is identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32810 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/7C7B1AE230C54565AB9DE410C476693D25": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology. Assistant Professor - Department of Psychology **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic-Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelors, masters, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The Colleges community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The Lehman College Department of Psychology invites applications for one or more full-time, tenure-track faculty members at the Assistant Professor rank. We encourage candidates to apply whose research is in any area of Clinical or Counseling Psychology. The start date is August 2027. Successful candidates must have a strong record of research and publication and a commitment both to seeking external funding and to undergraduate teaching. We are seeking candidates with an established program of research in any area of Clinical or Counseling Psychology. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active research program; seek external funding for their research; teach undergraduate classes in their area of expertise; mentor undergraduate students in research; advise students; provide service to the department, school, college, and university, e.g., committee, administrative, supervisory. Some in-person teachingis expected and some evening teaching may be needed. **QUALIFICATIONS** PhD in Clinical or Counseling Psychology or related field. Candidates must demonstrate effectiveness in teaching and communication, scholarly achievement, and collaborative potential.Preferred qualifications include a strong publication and funding record; an innovative program of research that would likely be of interest to our students; and a commitment to mentoring undergraduate students. There is the potential for joining the doctoral faculty of the CUNY Graduate Center to mentor PhD students through one of the psychology programs there. **COMPENSATION** $112,841 for a 9-month, full-time appointment. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Please submit the following documents collated into one PDF: (1) Cover letter (1 page) summarizing research interests in Clinical or Counseling Psychology, and potential synergies with ongoing research at CUNY and its collaborating institutions. (2) CV highlighting publications (with links), funding, and prior teaching/mentoring experience (3) Research Statement (2 pages) outlining experience, future goals and potential funding sources. (4) Teaching and Mentoring (2 pages) outlining experience, interests, and goals. (5) References (3) with contact information. Describe the nature of the relationship (e.g. PhD advisor, postdoctoral advisor, etc.). Letters will be requested after the applications are reviewed. **CLOSING DATE** Open until filled with review of applications to begin on September 30, 2026 **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32768 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/5170AD847549417386F30EF8060DBDD725": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (Tenure track) Adult Health Nursing",
      "description": "Assistant Professor (Tenure track) Adult Health Nursing. Assistant Professor (Tenure track) Adult Health Nursing **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Nursing at Lehman College, City University of New York, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Adult Health/Medical-Surgical Nursing beginning Spring 2027. Candidates must demonstrate a strong commitment to excellence in nursing education at the undergraduate and graduate levels and an active or developing program of research and scholarship consistent with their area of expertise. Teach undergraduate and graduate nursing courses in multiple modalities, including in-person, hybrid, and online formats. Teaching assignments may include daytime, evening, weekend and online courses based on departmental needs. Advise and mentor undergraduate, master's, and doctoral students. Maintain an active program of scholarship and dissemination appropriate to a tenure-track faculty appointment. Participate in curriculum development, program evaluation, and continuous quality improvement. Provide service to the Department, College, University, profession, and community. The Department of Nursing and is currently housed in the School of Health Sciences, Human Services and Nursing (HS2N). The School of Health Sciences, Human Services and Nursing currently includes six departments: Exercise Science and Recreation; Health Promotion and Nutrition Sciences; Health Equity, Administration & Technology; Social Work; Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences, and Nursing. The school is also home to the CUNY Institute for Health Equity. Departments in the School actively engage with community and government partners to support evidence-based practices and health equity, with a special emphasis on urban populations. The faculty are also strongly committed to high-quality teaching and preparation of ethical and skilled health and human service professionals. CAMPUS SPECIFIC POSITION DETAILS The Lehman College campus is located in the Bronx, New York and is a Senior College within the City University of New York (CUNY) system. Lehman is the only four-year public college in the Bronx and is recognized as a Hispanic-serving Institution. The college serves mainly undergraduate students preparing them for employment, the professions and further study. The Department of Nursing provides education for nursing students at the undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. The teaching load is 18 credit hours over a 9-month appointment. Student advisement is required, (minimum of 3 hours per week during the academic year). Attendance at staff development opportunities, as well as participation in department and school-wide meetings, is expected. The qualified candidate must perform additional service to the College, University, and community. This role includes spearheading program specific-professional development initiatives for undergraduate students. Undergraduate scholar mentorship is encouraged. Opportunities are available for faculty development and travel awards. Lehman College and CUNY internal funding is available through competitive grants for scholarship and professional development support. **QUALIFICATIONS** Ph.D., EdD., DNS degree with experience in Nursing or related discipline or a related academic field is required on commencement of the appointment. Must have a baccalaureate and master degree in nursing. Must be licensed or eligible for licensure in New York State at time of appointment. Strong evidence of successful teaching in adult health nursing. Demonstrated scholarship and dissemination of scholarship through publications and/or, presentations, etc. Ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Active involvement in professional organizations and sincere commitment to student success. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Clinical expertise and recent practice experience in adult health/medical-surgical nursing. College or university teaching experience in undergraduate and/or graduate nursing education. Experience with simulation, technology-enhanced learning, online/hybrid education, and/or innovative teaching strategies. Evidence of, or potential for, a sustained program of scholarship and dissemination. Experience with curriculum development, program evaluation, nursing accreditation, and/or continuous quality improvement. Experience mentoring students in scholarly, research, or evidence-based practice activities. Evidence of nurse leadership in accreditation, faculty professional development in leading nurse research teams **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor $109,025-$112,841. Salaries are commensurate with education and relevant experience and are subject to the Professional Staff Congress-CUNY salary schedule (http://www.psc-cuny.org/contract/psc-cuny-contract-salary-schedule). CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. CUNY also provides mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of a commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach a resume, cover letter, writing sample, and three professional references (name, title, organization, and contact information). For technical issues: Contact the service desk by email: service.desk@cuny.edu. If you can, provide screenshots. Please do not provide your User Account password; it is not needed to investigate any issue. For other questions: For questions about the content of any job posting, please contact the Human Resources department: human.resources@lehman.cuny.edu. **CLOSING DATE** Review of CVs will begin on October 30th for spring 2027 and continue until a candidate has been identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32924 Location: Lehman College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/F3216513B7EF4DAA999F29BFAEF6295C25": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Theatre, Dance, and Multimedia Performing Arts",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Theatre, Dance, and Multimedia Performing Arts. Assistant or Associate Professor - Theatre, Dance, and Multimedia Performing Arts **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Theatre, Dance, and Multimedia Performing Arts at Lehman College, City University of New York invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor or tenure-track / tenured Associate Professor position in Dramatic Writing beginning in the Fall of 2027. The department presents a full mainstage season of six productions, as well as having a multimedia performing arts track that integrates live performance with digital media that focuses on student-driven work as part of its mainstage season. In addition, the department has a focus on new work for the stage and screen created by students that is presented in various forums throughout the academic year. Full-time faculty are expected to mentor students in developing their own voices for a hybrid of stage and new media platforms. The department is seeking candidates with specializations in dramatic writing, including but not limited to playwriting, screenwriting, digital streaming media, immersive and devised theatre, merging traditional dramatic scriptwriting with new media storytelling arts. The department is seeking candidates that can combine the pedagogy of dramatic scriptwriting with an emphasis on performance, embodiment, and somatic learning that is the signature of the departments academic and performance work. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to teach major courses in playwriting and screenwriting at both the introductory and advanced levels. They must also be able to teach general education courses in theatre for non-majors. Depending upon the candidates area of specialization, they may be asked to teach other theatre program-related courses that cover new play development, public presentation and communication skills, business of the arts, and special topics in theatre, such as Africana Theatre and/or Latino Theatre. Candidates must be committed to exploring innovative pedagogical techniques to promote student success. To that end, candidates must be able to address the realities of teaching dramatic writing in the age of A.I. The cognitive offloading of creative, research, and technical skills to A.I. poses pedagogical questions regarding the authenticity of the individual voice and creative spirit of all students, and requires innovative teaching techniques as a result. Rather than ignoring A.I., how can pedagogy address the concerns posed by A.I. without simply saying no to its use? Candidates should be able to address both the drawbacks and possible uses of A.I. in their teaching with the search committee. The starting date is August 26, 2027. The teaching load is 18 credit hours (5-6 courses) per academic year that may be taught in person or online. The successful candidate will also be expected to maintain an active creative work/research agenda in the field. For tenure-track faculty, the teaching commitment is reduced by six courses over the first five years in order to assist with creative work/research. Tenured faculty may also receive teaching releases to assist with creative work/research. All faculty are eligible to apply for competitive internal Lehman College and CUNY grants to support their creative work/research. Service is required for all full-time faculty, and so the successful candidate will be expected to engage in significant service activities at the departmental, college, university, professional and/or community levels, commensurate with rank. Areas of service include but are not limited to recruitment, advising, curriculum development and assessment, and production supervision. The appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor will begin Fall 2027. Lehman College is a senior college in the City University of New York system that prides itself on its commitment to public urban higher education. Located in the Bronx, the College serves its diverse student body of more than 14,000 students by providing a liberal arts education that prepares them for employment, graduate study, and the professions. The College is a Hispanic-Serving Institution. In 2018, Lehman College was ranked 3rd in the U.S. among four-year public institutions for economic mobility for students, and 1st in the U.S. among Hispanic-Serving Institutions with high extended upward income mobility rates. **QUALIFICATIONS** MFA in Dramatic Writing or PhD/DFA in Theatre by the start date of the position (August 26th, 2027). **COMPENSATION** Assistant Prof: $94,017-$105,588 Associate Prof: $113,745-$125,436 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** For a list of all jobs available at CUNY, visit the following page: https://cuny.jobs/ Visit https://www.cuny.edu/employment/, sign in if you already have an account or register as a New User account if you do not, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply for Job\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must upload a Curriculum Vitae, a Cover Letter, a Dramatic Writing Sample (no more than 10,000 words), a brief Creative Work/Research Statement (1-2 pages), evidence of teaching excellence and interest in innovative pedagogy, and the names of three (3) professional references name, title, organization, and contact information who are familiar with the candidates record of teaching and/or creative work/research. The three (3) professional references must be included in the original application to be considered. If an initial interview is requested, potential interviewees must arrange to have three (3) letters of reference submitted two weeks prior to their interview date. For technical issues: Contact the service desk by email: service.desk@cuny.edu. If you can, provide screenshots. Please do not provide your User Account password; it is not needed to investigate any issue. For questions about the content of any job posting, please contact the Human Resources department: Human.Resources@lehman.cuny.edu. **CLOSING DATE** Please submit completed applications by November 28, 2026 for full consideration. Review of applications will begin on November 30, and continue until a candidate has been identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32829 Location: Lehman College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/03113E06CA7943E78D1FFDFA19C532D425": {
      "title": "Social Work Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure or Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Social Work Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure or Tenure Track). Social Work Assistant/Associate Professor (Tenure or Tenure Track) **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Social Work invites applications for two tenure or tenure-track Assistant or Associate professorship beginning Fall 2027. Candidates must have an active record of research/scholarship/creative works, and a strong commitment to teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The successful candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate and graduate level courses in social work practice, human behavior in the social environment, social policy, and fieldwork, engage in research/scholarship and professional organization, advise students, provide service to the department, college, university, and community, i.e. program coordination, committee, administrative, supervisory, and other assignments normally associated with a full-time tenure or tenure-track academic appointment, evening teaching will be required. The Assistant/Associate Professor will report directly to the chair of the department of Social Work. Essential Duties and responsibilities: The ability to support the Mission and antiracism lens of the Social Work Department The ability to teach and engage students in critical thinking on the undergraduate and/graduate level successfully, with a commitment to student learning. Willingness to adapt to varied teaching modalities including the use of technology re: hybrid, in person, and online Curriculum development capacity in one or more of the core areas: practice, policy, research, field work and electives Demonstrated capacity scholarship, research and grantsmanship Collegiality and the ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. Active involvement in service at the Department, school, university, community & professional organizations. CAMPUS SPECIFIC POSITION DETAILS The Lehman College campus is located in the Bronx, New York and is a Senior College within the City University of New York (CUNY) system. Lehman is the only four-year public college in the Bronx and is recognized as a Hispanic-serving Institution. The college serves mainly undergraduate students preparing them for employment, the professions and further study. The Department of Social Work provides education for social work students at the undergraduate and graduate levels. The teaching load is 18 credit hours over a 9-month appointment. Student advisement is required, (minimum of 3 hours per week during the academic year). Attendance at staff development opportunities, as well as participation in department and school-wide meetings, is expected. The qualified candidate must perform additional service to the College, University, and community. Undergraduate scholar mentorship is encouraged. Opportunities are available for faculty development and travel awards. Lehman College and CUNY internal funding is available through competitive grants for scholarship and professional development support. The Social Work Programs at Lehman College, both the undergraduate and graduate programs, are fully accredited by the Council on Social Work Education. The mission of both programs is to serve under-served urban communities and populations. We have a strong commitment to urban communities such the Bronx and to the ideals of social and economic justice. We have strong ties to the urban community and a deep commitment to our students. The Department of Social Work is currently housed in the School of Health Sciences, Human Services and Nursing (HS2N). The School of Health Sciences, Human Services and Nursing currently includes six departments: Exercise Science and Recreation; Health Promotion and Nutrition Sciences; Health Equity, Administration & Technology; Social Work; Speech, Language and Hearing Sciences, and Nursing. The school is also home to the CUNY Institute for Health Equity. Departments in the School actively engage with community and government partners to support evidence-based practices and health equity, with a special emphasis on urban populations. The faculty are also strongly committed to high quality teaching and preparation of ethical and skilled health and human service professionals. **QUALIFICATIONS** For Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor: DSW or Ph.D. in Social Work with experience in agency-based practice required on commencement of the appointment. Preferred Qualifications: Three years of post-masters practice experience; Experience with diverse populations and urban issues. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor $ 109,025 - $112,841 Associate Professor $ $118,070-$122,202 Salaries are commensurate with education and relevant experience and are subject to the Professional Staff Congress-CUNY salary schedule (http://www.psc-cuny.org/contract/psc-cuny-contract-salary-schedule). CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach a resume, cover letter, writing sample, and three professional references (name, title, organization, and contact information). For technical issues: Contact the service desk by email: service.desk@cuny.edu. If you can, provide screenshots. Please do not provide your User Account password; it is not needed to investigate any issue. For other questions: For questions about the content of any job posting, please contact the Human Resources department: human.resources@lehman.cuny.edu **CLOSING DATE** Review of CVs will begin on February 15 for Fall 2027 and continue until a candidate has been identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32902 Location: Lehman College"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/05F89680C8A64EB0AA4C955E9C7A014325": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - Speech-Language-Hearing Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - Speech-Language-Hearing Sciences. Assistant Professor or Associate Professor - Speech-Language-Hearing Sciences **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** Lehman College of the City University of New York invites applications for a full-time (9-month) tenure-track Assistant professor tenured or tenure-track or an Associate professor tenured or tenure-track position in the Department of Speech-Language-Hearing Sciences. Applicants must hold an earned Ph.D. in communication sciences and disorders or a related discipline, and preferably hold ASHA CCC-SLP and be eligible for NYS licensure. The successful candidate must have an active record of scholarship and a strong commitment to teaching communication sciences and disorders at the undergraduate and graduate levels to culturally and linguistically diverse students. Lehman College is a four-year senior college and one of 25 colleges in the City University of New York (CUNY). Located in the Bronx, NY, Lehman is a Hispanic-Serving Institution and serves over 10,000 undergraduate and graduate students. The Department of Speech-Language-Hearing Sciences enrolls an average of 350 undergraduate and 100-125 graduate students each year. The teaching load is 18 credit hours over a 9-month appointment. Opportunities exist to teach undergraduate and graduate courses, supervise graduate clinicians, and collaborate with other CUNY faculty in research. Service to the college, university and community is part of the mission as is a clear commitment to student engagement including advisement. Teaching is reduced for junior faculty over the first five years for scholarly development and all faculty are actively encouraged to seek external funding. Opportunities are available for faculty development and travel awards. Lehman College and CUNY internal funding is available through competitive grants for scholarship and professional development support. Faculty are expected to maintain a regular on campus presence for teaching, office hours, departmental and other activities. You may be assigned to teach evenings and/or weekends and/or online, either synchronously or asynchronously. This is not a remote position. **QUALIFICATIONS** QUALIFICATIONS: Ph.D. degree in Communication Disorders and Sciences or an equivalent. Evidence of an established or developing scholarly agenda. The ability to teach successfully, demonstrated scholarship or achievement, and ability to cooperate with others for the good of the institution. PREFERED QUALIFICATIONS: Certificate of Clinical Competency from the American Speech-Language-Hearing Association Evidence of a successful record of college-level teaching experience in online, hybrid and/or in-person modalities Clinical experience in speech-language pathology as well as in supervision. Experience advising undergraduate students and supervising practicum work and fieldwork Clinical or teaching experience with linguistically and culturally diverse populations Expertise in fluency, dysphagia, speech science, motor speech disorders, audiology, or alternative and augmentative communication (AAC) is a plus. Bilingual is a desirable skill for the position. **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor $102,460 - $112,841 Associate Professor $122,202 - $133,558 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates must attach the following documents: + A letter of interest + A curriculum vitae including the names, titles, organizations, and contact information for three professorial references + A copy of unofficial transcripts for the terminal degree completed + A research statement including concrete descriptions of current and future plans for research (up to 2 pages) + A teaching statement including evidence of your ability to generate equitable opportunities for learning for students from diverse backgrounds (up to 2 pages) **CLOSING DATE** Review of applications will begin late October 2026 through November 30, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32979 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/028AAD664A314D83973C01F33E9AA38425": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Computer Science. Assistant Professor - Computer Science **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** Lehman College, of The City University of New York, ranks among the top five institutions in the nation for fostering social mobility. A four-year Hispanic-Serving Institution in the Bronx, Lehman offers bachelors, masters, and advanced degrees and certificate programs in the Liberal Arts, sciences, and professions. The Colleges community-driven mission and notable academic programs attract a diverse, international enrollment of over 15,000 students who take courses on its 37-acre, tree-lined campus and online degree programs. Many thousands more community members benefit yearly from its active cultural, educational, health, and economic outreach programs and services. The Department of Computer Science consists of six tenured faculty and three lecturers, with plans to expand further in the coming years. The department offers undergraduate degrees in Computer Science, Computer Information Systems, and in Data Science as well as an MS in Computer Science. Through a joint appointment on the Graduate Center Doctoral Faculty, the successful candidate can teach and advise PhD students. The Department has a strong focus on undergraduate education. Our undergraduates are well prepared for jobs and internships or to pursue graduate education. Lehman College of The City University of New York invites applications for an Assistant Professor beginning Fall 2027. Outstanding candidates from all areas of computer science and closely related fields will be considered, however, those working in the following research areas are particularly encouraged to apply: Data Center-Scale Computing, Data Science, Machine Learning, Networks, Robotics, and Scientific and High-Performance Computing. The successful candidate will be expected to develop and maintain an active research program; seek external funding for their research; teach undergraduate and graduate classes in their area of expertise and beyond; mentor undergraduate students in research; advise students; provide service to the department, school, college, and university, e.g., committee, administrative, supervisory. Some in-person teaching is expected and some evening teaching may be needed. **QUALIFICATIONS** A PhD in Computer Science or a closely related field is required. Current and past faculty backgrounds include computer science, mathematics, operations research, and electrical engineering. We encourage applications from candidates from these and similar disciplines whose scholarly focus is strongly concentrated in those areas of their discipline closely aligned with computer science. Candidates must demonstrate the ability to conduct high-quality research and the potential to develop and sustain an active research agenda. Strong pedagogical skills and talent are essential, along with the versatility to teach a broad range of the undergraduate and graduate computer science courses offered by Lehman College. A sincere commitment to students, effective communication skills, and the ability to collaborate constructively with colleagues are required. **COMPENSATION** $112,841 CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit www.cuny.edu, access the employment page, log in or create a new user account, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply Now\" and provide the requested information. Candidates should provide a CV/resume and statement of scholarly interests. **CLOSING DATE** Review of applications will begin on November 30th, 2026. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 33000 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/6C8C96424DCC4255B2D6E1B9418F952225": {
      "title": "Lecturer, Studio Art Foundations and Art Education",
      "description": "Lecturer, Studio Art Foundations and Art Education. Lecturer, Studio Art Foundations and Art Education **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Department of Art at Lehman College invites applications for a Lecturer position in Studio Art Foundations and Art Education with teaching and department service responsibilities, to start in fall 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to teach studio art foundation courses (i.e., Basic Drawing, Introduction to 2D/3D Design, etc.), art education methods, and other courses as assigned consistent with the candidate's qualifications, in addition to coordinating the graduate Art Education program and working in conjunction with the School of Education on undergraduate majors paired in the Art Education pathway for grades Pre K12, advising and providing support to students seeking NYSED initial teacher certification. We are seeking an artist-educator who is student-centered and will work collaboratively across campus and the community. **Responsibilities:** Annual workload of 24 course hours, including teaching studio art foundations and art education courses during the fall and spring semesters commensurate with the candidates qualifications; advising, recruitment, mentorship, and guidance of Art Education students, as well as program and course assessment and other service to the department, school, college, and university as needed. Teaching assignments may include evening, weekend, in-person, and online courses, utilizing multimedia and instructional technologies as appropriate. + Supervise, mentor, and evaluate student teachers in PreK12 settings. + Instructors are expected to plan and deliver theoretical instruction as well as field-based or studio-based experiences aligned with the programs mission, objectives, and curriculum. + Candidate must demonstrate sensitivity to the educational needs of students from diverse population, andmust be committed to exploring innovative pedagogical techniques to promote student success. Candidates must be able to address the realities of teaching in the age of A.I., and should be able toaddress both the drawbacks and possible uses (if any) of A.I. in their teaching with the search committee. **QUALIFICATIONS** **Required Qualifications:** + Masters degree in Art Education and/or MFA in Art completed by the start of the Fall 2027 semester, and either a BA in Art Education or a BFA in Art + Minimum of three (3) years of teaching experience in a PreK12 art classroom, including experience working with diverse student populations + Demonstrated ability to teach Art Education courses, including fundamentals of art education, curriculum and assessment, methods for teaching art, and to supervise student teaching + College-level teaching experience in art education and/or studio art **Preferred Qualifications** + PhD in Art Education by the start of the Fall 2027 semester + New York State Art Teacher certification + Five (5) or more years of teaching experience in a New York City Department of Education Pre K12 art classroom **COMPENSATION** Lecturer: $87,149 - $98,638 Lecturer (Doctoral Schedule): $93,080 - $111,455 Salary is commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** **Upload the following as one attachment:** + Letter of intent + Curriculum Vitae + One-page artist statement + One-page statement of teaching philosophy, including examples of student mentorship + Sample syllabi for studio art foundations and art education courses + 20 images of applicant's work clearly labeled with title, media/technique, size, year + 20 images of student work captioned with title, media, size, year, and level + Three professional references, including names, email and phone (semi-finalists: references will be sent a link to upload a letter of recommendation) We encourage you to apply even if you do not meet every preferred qualification. We are most interested in finding the candidate who will best contribute to our Department and the University. For a list of all jobs available at CUNY, visit the following page: https://cuny.jobs/ Visit https://www.cuny.edu/employment/, sign in if you already have an account or register a New User account if you do not, and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Title. Select \"Apply for Job\" and provide the requested information. For more instructions on applying for a job at CUNY, see https://www.cuny.edu/employment/system-instructions/applying/ Candidates must upload a cover letter, a curriculum vitae (that includes the names of three professional references name, title, organization, and contact information), and a statement of teaching. In addition, candidates should arrange for three (3) letters of recommendation to be sent to the search committee at Lehmanartlecturer@lehman.cuny.edu . For technical issues, please contact the service desk by email: service.desk@cuny.edu. If you can, provide screenshots. Please do not provide your User Account password; it is not needed to investigate any issue. For questions about the content of any job posting, please contact the Human Resources department: recruiting@lehman.cuny.edu **CLOSING DATE** Please submit completed applications by January 2, 2027 for full consideration. Review of C.V.s will begin on January 4 and continue until a candidate has been identified. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32977 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    },
    "https://cuny.jobs/ABB1AEBFA71A4D0C84B2A33CA39D5D6125": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Art, Sculpture/New Media",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Art, Sculpture/New Media. Assistant Professor of Art, Sculpture/New Media **FACULTY VACANCY ANNOUNCEMENT** The Art Department at Lehman College, City University of New York seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor or tenure-track/tenured Associate Professor position in Art to teach within the Sculpture/New Media specialization. Lehman College is the City University of New Yorks Bronx senior college. This is a full-time position with an anticipated start date for the 2027-2028 academic year. It offers full CUNY benefits that are among the most comprehensive in the country. Responsibilities for CUNY senior college tenure-track faculty positions generally include teaching two to three classes per semester. The lead faculty member in the sculpture area will teach a range of materials and techniques, and will work with students at a wide range of levels, from introductory sculpture for art majors and non-art majors, to advanced undergraduate and graduate courses (including thesis supervision) in sculpture, new media and/or time-based media. The ideal candidate is an innovative artist-educator with an expansive contemporary creative practice, who is qualified to teach all levels of sculpture, new media and/or time-based media courses within a department that offers Art BA, BFA, BS, MA, and MFA degree programs in an urban campus setting. Additionally, the successful candidate understands interdisciplinary approaches to sculpture and new media, including traditional and digital methods; is engaged with critical contemporary issues; possesses a deep and expansive understanding of the history and theory of contemporary art; maintains an active studio practice; has a significant exhibition record; and has the ability to foster a welcoming and inclusive studio environment. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to assume leadership and mentorship with students, and conduct a collaborative, team-oriented approach to pedagogy. They will have the ability to weave their vision of the future of the sculpture-new media area into the Art Departments curriculum. Candidates must demonstrate sensitivity to the educational needs of students from diverse populations, and must be committed to exploring innovative pedagogical techniques to promote student success. Candidates should be able to address the realities of teaching in the age of A.I., and should be able to address both the drawbacks and possible uses (if any) of A.I. in their teaching with the search committee. In addition to ongoing excellence in teaching and creative/scholarly research, a prominent exhibition record, and professional activities, the position requires regular service to the Art Department, School of Arts & Humanities, Lehman College, City University of New York, and the community. This includes academic departmental student advising, and committee work. **QUALIFICATIONS** **Required Qualifications** : + M.F.A. (or equivalent) in Sculpture, New Media, Time-based media or related media + Minimum of three years of college-level teaching experience + Expertise with a wide range of conceptual and technical approaches to art production + Conversant in contemporary practices and critical issues in sculpture, new media, and/or time-based media + Demonstrated commitment to creating cross-media, interdisciplinary, and high-impact learning opportunities **Preferred Qualifications** : + Possesses a broad intellectual approach to contemporary art practice + Has a record of mentoring and connecting students to career opportunities + Demonstrates a commitment to integrating sustainable practices into the sculpture studio and curriculum + Incorporates into course curriculum emergent digital technologies such as digital fabrication technologies and interactive media + Has an interest in a wide range of sculptural practices including installation and performance + Has an engaged, robust artistic practice that further expands the field of contemporary art **COMPENSATION** Assistant Professor: $94,017-$105,588 Salary is commensurate with education and experience. CUNY offers faculty a competitive compensation and benefits package covering health insurance, pension and retirement benefits, paid parental leave, and savings programs. We also provide mentoring and support for research, scholarship, and publication as part of our commitment to ongoing faculty professional development. **HOW TO APPLY** Visit https://cuny.jobs/ and search for this vacancy using the Job ID or Job Title and select \"Apply Now\". Sign in if you already have an account or register as a New User account if you do not. Select Apply for Job and provide the requested information. Candidates must upload a letter of intent, curriculum vitae, one-page artist statement, one-page teaching philosophy, 20 images of work, and the names of three professional references (include name, title, organization, and contact information) who may subsequently be contacted for letters of recommendation. These letters should include the Job ID# in the email or the body of the letter and are to be sent to the Chair of the Search Committee (email address forthcoming). For technical issues contact the service desk at CUNY by email: service.desk@cuny.edu. If you can, provide screenshots. Please do not provide your User Account password; it is not needed to investigate any issue. For questions about the content of this job posting, please contact the Human Resources department at Lehman College: Human.Resources@lehman.cuny.edu. For questions about the areas of research in this job posting or about courses offered by the Department of Art please contact the Chair of the Search Committee (email address forthcoming). **Upload the following as one attachment:** Letter of intent Curriculum Vitae One-page artist statement One-page statement of teaching philosophy, including examples of student mentorship Sample syllabus 20 images of applicant's work clearly labeled with title, media/technique, size, year (Semi-finalists: 20 images of student work captioned with title, media, size, year) Three professional references, including names, email and phone (semi-finalists: references will be sent a link to upload a letter of recommendation) **CLOSING DATE** Review of applications will begin January 25, 2027. **JOB SEARCH CATEGORY** CUNY Job Posting: Faculty **EQUAL EMPLOYMENT OPPORTUNITY** CUNY encourages people with disabilities, minorities, veterans and women to apply. At CUNY, Italian Americans are also included among our protected groups. Applicants and employees will not be discriminated against on the basis of any legally protected category, including sexual orientation or gender identity. EEO/AA/Vet/Disability Employer. Job ID: 32990 Location: Lehman College Job Type: Full-Time"
    }
  },
